that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+6y+(z-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}+6y+9)+(z-1)^{2} & =16+9 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2}={5}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-70560"] :question/problem "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=(\\sqrt{2})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(0,-3,1)$ and the radius $r=\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-70650/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "3f326182-ca89-5d36-8b2a-be56f652957a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70650/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "f8128909-66c7-5afe-8596-fc67fe12f8cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70650/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "57aeb756-9c5f-536c-98e2-a76517d566e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70650/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "384006ed-8187-5e6d-a37c-304da48e4136" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70650/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b8ecb18d-33aa-5f20-bb98-ef68a955bbc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70650/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b465e7f-7999-5afe-bb46-dbb70c1c98c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70650/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-70650/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-70650/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-70650/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" "q-70650/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-70650/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70650" :question/id #uuid "361d563b-06bb-5688-be7a-668acbcfa976" :question/math-academy-id "q-70650" :question/problem "What is the radius of the sphere ${x}^{2}+4x+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2}=12?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4x+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2} & =12 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+4x+4)+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2} & =12+4 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2}={4}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164251/selection/e3bf4c2f6de708c9310580ebbeb3251cc333f7070e731c9ee6aae109dc48d931" :answer/id #uuid "77546191-1b7f-5baa-874d-a4e9318fb0ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,0,0)$ and $(2,0,0).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164251/selection/d29a8a64a29442b8158a08d96fddf36b7582a6dd9be9e27d14267e30d6ddf592" :answer/id #uuid "57f9e0dc-6c1d-5479-b4c5-05ab74aff856" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164251/selection/3ba5315a8deff9be9ee07e4a50976f5154afa1531a0ca6c8e688961e07c823f5" :answer/id #uuid "c28ea49c-006e-5e92-860f-d94069085acf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-4,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164251/selection/9a58f1387b07e8da542fc0d81e08359051be3f4e7432e9186d7743ab3e83f4e3" :answer/id #uuid "6f19da9a-a976-55db-ba1b-0bb043ee255b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,0,0)$ and $(0,0,0).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164251/selection/60c8432a0465ccd361d275f477124d5d6b6794792ab53bd180010646189702d9" :answer/id #uuid "6526dcd7-cf3b-5749-97e9-4f5b36759956" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(2,0,0).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164251/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4080cdc1-f4d2-50fe-88c6-c80150fc91fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164251/selection/d29a8a64a29442b8158a08d96fddf36b7582a6dd9be9e27d14267e30d6ddf592" :answer-field/choices ["q-164251/selection/e3bf4c2f6de708c9310580ebbeb3251cc333f7070e731c9ee6aae109dc48d931" "q-164251/selection/d29a8a64a29442b8158a08d96fddf36b7582a6dd9be9e27d14267e30d6ddf592" "q-164251/selection/3ba5315a8deff9be9ee07e4a50976f5154afa1531a0ca6c8e688961e07c823f5" "q-164251/selection/9a58f1387b07e8da542fc0d81e08359051be3f4e7432e9186d7743ab3e83f4e3" "q-164251/selection/60c8432a0465ccd361d275f477124d5d6b6794792ab53bd180010646189702d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164251" :question/id #uuid "8358ba3d-fe0d-5487-9222-565dc3b520a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-164251" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4}=1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=0$ and $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164251/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164251"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71118/selection/9a065cb229e578b871973f87f4642498edceb74ffbc31b1b31e3511cf9188930" :answer/id #uuid "df166535-abb6-5754-9b30-14b9515c509e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,0,\\frac{11}{6})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71118/selection/9cfc4e6016e5a1c5467f07ebdcfc54d7b19eaf6f7feb7f7ac0a45f4716847f67" :answer/id #uuid "d095a839-e3d2-5dea-a229-9ef40be25094" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,-\\frac{11}{6})$ and $(0,0,\\frac{11}{6})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71118/selection/7ea90e8411dabff28fcc85e3f85e515723d5b10bba0a27238a667a19f51a8087" :answer/id #uuid "d563285b-f63c-569d-b098-93c69288680c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,\\frac{11}{6})$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71118/selection/a711de27ba21d6d70ae6539f673b73df5588b65d890a72c39d2903e0b616e23c" :answer/id #uuid "57b14a7b-dd6e-553c-9c26-5c7dc839b29f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,-\\sqrt{11})$ and $(0,0,\\sqrt{11})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71118/selection/a43a88d369550433276a114bbe7524a7124a2a4c741b9afb2ae110442ae78d8b" :answer/id #uuid "e5fabc7d-c617-50a8-933a-8bda692196f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71118/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4d2658-5b5a-5aed-aa5e-9322ded6faf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71118/selection/9cfc4e6016e5a1c5467f07ebdcfc54d7b19eaf6f7feb7f7ac0a45f4716847f67" :answer-field/choices ["q-71118/selection/9a065cb229e578b871973f87f4642498edceb74ffbc31b1b31e3511cf9188930" "q-71118/selection/9cfc4e6016e5a1c5467f07ebdcfc54d7b19eaf6f7feb7f7ac0a45f4716847f67" "q-71118/selection/7ea90e8411dabff28fcc85e3f85e515723d5b10bba0a27238a667a19f51a8087" "q-71118/selection/a711de27ba21d6d70ae6539f673b73df5588b65d890a72c39d2903e0b616e23c" "q-71118/selection/a43a88d369550433276a114bbe7524a7124a2a4c741b9afb2ae110442ae78d8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71118" :question/id #uuid "6d29c492-0ca8-561c-9ff3-546ae9bcb878" :question/math-academy-id "q-71118" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{11}=1$, find its intercepts with the $z$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{11} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{11} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{z}^{2}}{11} & =\\frac{11}{36} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =\\frac{121}{36} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{11}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-\\frac{11}{6}$ and $z=\\frac{11}{6}.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-\\frac{11}{6})$ and $(0,0,\\frac{11}{6}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71118/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71118"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73190/selection/ac0650ab30b84a13aaffd852a36ca752477e642246e5cb456600d164c4ad8511" :answer/id #uuid "4c49531e-882a-5825-9917-3231652dd4fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-4,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73190/selection/ec6035020da96ec41f2719494e71ad155be727807362d05fc09abd3cbfcaa884" :answer/id #uuid "f63bc0f1-3bd8-5ca5-ab72-36dbf9250031" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-3\\sqrt{2},0,0)$ and $(3\\sqrt{2},0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73190/selection/7080a6c22ee5a522983ec7b9564b43caadbc729e3cbd24017dfbb515c3d32769" :answer/id #uuid "a3c06e65-98d2-5e45-a44c-9fd61df94696" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73190/selection/3cae761720c167e0433907483448b8f3369131d7c071d38a48bd4666accac233" :answer/id #uuid "1eb96635-4614-5a23-8bca-1f41d63ed2c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(2,0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73190/selection/c8b30d1b7bff64a69563614dbbeebe81e32781d0995f0252b33b87ffb9aa60e3" :answer/id #uuid "0fba62fc-af7e-5b7c-92b4-67530b459b05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(4,0,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73190/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "16d75cdf-6f3a-5212-bef0-1af4bed23b41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73190/selection/7080a6c22ee5a522983ec7b9564b43caadbc729e3cbd24017dfbb515c3d32769" :answer-field/choices ["q-73190/selection/ac0650ab30b84a13aaffd852a36ca752477e642246e5cb456600d164c4ad8511" "q-73190/selection/ec6035020da96ec41f2719494e71ad155be727807362d05fc09abd3cbfcaa884" "q-73190/selection/7080a6c22ee5a522983ec7b9564b43caadbc729e3cbd24017dfbb515c3d32769" "q-73190/selection/3cae761720c167e0433907483448b8f3369131d7c071d38a48bd4666accac233" "q-73190/selection/c8b30d1b7bff64a69563614dbbeebe81e32781d0995f0252b33b87ffb9aa60e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73190" :question/id #uuid "fc3f69db-faba-5b23-aeec-3cea350fe1f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73190" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{1}{2}+0 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =9 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =1\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=4$ and $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(-2,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73190/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73190"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164275/selection/adb44819a16284a186a6e42fa4e430bcf8c44ae91094ee448a477bcc21643c5b" :answer/id #uuid "4f31cdba-31ec-569a-846f-af04267fa44a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164275/selection/155e81d861f50f6eb9d94aad86ff0e46638856676a793c75416071afc74ff2fb" :answer/id #uuid "c62fd80a-e615-5dd7-8d53-16db17180b29" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,-16)$ and $(0,0,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164275/selection/d3a42bd6748e883162ebd53b6